{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Perhaps.</b> It occurs with many meanings, likewise \"perhaps a stranger may do\" (Hosea 8:7)." "The he of הֶהָשֵׁב is opened with a small pataḥ because there is a construct he with a kamatz, and if it were opened with a large pataḥ it would be heavy on the tongue."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:32.456916256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}